node_modules/
dist/
.env
.env.local
*.log
.DS_Store
.vite/
migrations/meta/
data/kb/*.embeddings.json

# Generated deliverables. `npx tsx scripts/build-cases-pdf.ts` writes them and
# `npx tsx scripts/build-promo-video.ts` writes the MP4s; both read their
# content out of shared/ modules, so the repository holds the recipe and not
# twenty megabytes of output per rebuild. docs/case-studies.pdf predates this
# rule and is still tracked.
docs/*.pdf
!docs/case-studies.pdf
docs/*.docx
docs/promo/*.mp4

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT IN THE PUBLIC REPOSITORY.
#
# This repository is the fork target and is going public. These five documents
# are how this company prices, what it earns, which tier each offer sits in and
# who invoices whom — commercially useful to a competitor and to the partner,
# and useful to nobody who wants to run a copy. The engineering documents in
# docs/ stay, because a forker needs them.
#
# They are still HERE, so an agent working in this checkout reads them at
# private/<name> — every pointer in the code and in parcels.json was moved with
# them. Keep them in their own repository; this one must never see them again.
private/
